description:
For an international organization in Europe, we are urgently looking for a Full REMOTE Network Engineer.










 EU candidates are welcome to apply and be based in Europe. Work permit is not provided. This position is long\-term. Candidates need to be fluent in English. Candidates need to be willing to go on\-site for local meetings.










**Tasks and Responsibilities** 



* Review existing network architecture in affected offices, including core, access, firewall, and wireless components;
* Validate identified risks related to EOL/EOS equipment and operational dependencies;
* Design a target\-state network architecture aligned with standards and Cisco Meraki best practices;
* Define migration and transition architectures minimizing service disruption;
* Provide technical leadership for the replacement of Budapest core switches and firewalls;
* Support configuration, deployment, and cutover activities for Meraki\-based infrastructure;
* Assist with phased renewal planning for Geneva access switching and wireless infrastructure;
* Ensure proper VLAN, routing, firewall, and Wi\-Fi design and configuration;
* Provide technical leadership for the replacement of core switches and firewalls;
* Support configuration, deployment, and cutover activities for Meraki\-based infrastructure;
* Assist with phased renewal planning for access switching and wireless infrastructure;
* Ensure proper VLAN, routing, firewall, and Wi\-Fi design and configuration;
* Produce high\-quality network documentation (diagrams, configurations, BOMs);
* Document operational runbooks and handover materials;
* Provide knowledge transfer sessions to internal teams;
* Provide risk and dependency analysis for decision\-making and steering committees;









 Profile:



* Bachelor or Master degree;
* \+5 years of proven experience as a Network Engineer or Network Architect in enterprise environments;
* Strong expertise with Cisco networking technologies, including:



 Layer 2/3 switching;




 Routing, VLANs, and DHCP;




 Firewalling and site\-to\-site VPNs;



* Hands\-on experience with Cisco Meraki (MX, MS, MR) in production environments;
* Solid understanding of network security principles and best practices;
* Experience with network lifecycle management (EOL/EOS planning);
* Experience in hybrid or globally distributed organizations;
* Experience transitioning from managed network services to in\-house or cloud\-managed solutions;
* Fluent in English;
